      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Rupture of the deep transverse metacarpal ligament (DTML) can result in pain, impaired grip strength, and undermine functional performance of the hand. We describe the case of a patient whose right hand came into contact with a boat propeller. He sustained a complete disruption of the DTML between the second and third ray in addition to soft tissue injury and open metacarpal fractures. Although other techniques describe a reconstruction of the DTML, our technique describes an adjunctive technique that strongly augments the A1 pulley reconstruction and nullifies the requirements of palmaris longus graft."},
